Final instruction

Implement these changes as strict universal rules of Alva’s combat and movement systems, not as manually applied tweaks to a few existing attacks.

The guiding distinction is:

Step-in is automatic movement belonging to an eligible grounded melee attack. Attack Steering is directional movement controlled by the fighter during an eligible move.

Aerial attacks and object-based moves must not receive automatic Step-in. Specials and 3/5-second cooldown moves must not receive generic Attack Steering.

In every category, deliberately authored movement behavior takes precedence over a newly introduced generic default.

Above all, the human player and CPU must operate under exactly the same rules. The CPU must understand the movement, simulate it accurately, and be capable of using it in real combat.
